  "notes": "REGISTER: Childish but widely used. The standard term when talking to or about children, pets, and in casual conversation among adults.\n\nVARIANT: うんこ is a rougher/cruder variant with the same meaning.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- うんちする (to poop)\n- うんちが{出|で}る (to have a bowel movement)\n\nALTERNATIVES: More formal terms include {大便|だいべん} (clinical) and {便|べん} (medical). Polite euphemisms include お{通|つう}じ (bowel movement) and {大|おお}きい{方|ほう} (lit. 'the big one').",
